@page "/about"
<h1>About Karamel-Web</h1>
<p>Karamel-Web is a browser-based karaoke player built with Blazor WebAssembly. It keeps your media files on your machine while enabling multi-device sessions.</p>
<p>Karamel and Karamel-Web are developed by Dominik Damerow (akrostichon).</p>

<h2>Third-Party Libraries & Attributions</h2>
<ul>
  <li>CDGraphics.js — used for CDG rendering. License: MIT. <a href="https://github.com/bhj/cdgraphics">https://github.com/bhj/cdgraphics</a></li>
  <li>jsmediatags — used for ID3 tag extraction. License: LGPL-3.0. <a href="https://github.com/aadsm/jsmediatags">https://github.com/aadsm/jsmediatags</a></li>
  <li>QRCode.js — used for QR code generation. License: MIT. <a href="https://github.com/davidshimjs/qrcodejs">https://github.com/davidshimjs/qrcodejs</a></li>
  <li>JSZip — used for ZIP file enumeration/extraction. License: MIT. <a href="https://github.com/Stuk/jszip">https://github.com/Stuk/jszip</a></li>
  <li>microsoft/signalr — SignalR client for real-time communication. License: MIT. <a href="https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore/tree/main/src/SignalR/clients/ts/signalr">https://github.com/dotnet/aspnetcore</a></li>
  <li>Fluxor — state management for Blazor. License: MIT. <a href="https://github.com/mrpmorris/Fluxor">https://github.com/mrpmorris/Fluxor</a></li>
</ul>

<p>All third-party JavaScript libraries used by Karamel-Web are hosted locally under <code>wwwroot/lib/</code> and
are loaded from the application itself (no external CDN requests are made at runtime).</p>

